      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T18:51:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m against hardcoding a number that we have obtained by running a test on a particular effect implementation. We should either hardcode `-3.0` which is the theoretical RMS for a sine wave with amplitude equaling the full digital scale, or we should apply `audio_utils_compute_power_mono` to an input sine wave with the amplitude `1.0` (not `kMaxAudioSampleValue`!), which should give us a close value.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 261,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 264,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "dbc207b99a911ef78e2b3f3f6ef3baa4b9925e86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbbfbb15_91cd12a9",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/vts/VtsHalVisualizerTargetTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T18:51:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks inconsistent. We take `maxAudioSampleValue` from `testMaxAudioSampleValueList` where it can be scaled by `kMaxAudioSampleValue`. But the keys in `maxAudioSampleRms/PeakMap` do not have this scaling. Thus, this test currently only works when `kMaxAudioSampleValue \u003d\u003d 1`.\n\nI don\u0027t think we need to make these map lookups at all. We can just define a structure which contains the amplitude and the associated expected values.\n\nHowever, the overall approach of having these predefined expected values has a flaw because a change in `kMaxAudioSampleValue` will invalidate them. I would also recommend calculating them from the input, not taking from our measurements. In fact, I\u0027ve looked at the `-633` value for the RMS of the 1.0 input, and suspected that we had provided a wrong input to the effect, please see my comment below about stereo/mono discrepancy.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 265,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 272,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "dbc207b99a911ef78e2b3f3f6ef3baa4b9925e86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
